*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Molecule: H2O (asymmetric geometry)
* Basis: 6-31G
* Symmetry: C1
* Features tested: Analytic SS-MC-PDFT gradients with the hybrid meta-GGA
*                  on-top functional tM06-L, lambda = 0.25, without (NoCD) and
*                  with (RICD) Cholesky decomposition, singlet and triplet
* Responsible person: Bhavnesh Jangid, University of Chicago, 2026
* Comments: The analytic gradients agree with central finite differences of
*           the hybrid MC-PDFT energy to about 1e-5 Eh/bohr. Starting orbitals
*           are the converged CAS(2,2) singlet and triplet ones (the SCF guess
*           ends in a saddle point, and the singlet orbitals do not converge the
*           triplet reliably with all compilers).
*           The finite-difference comparison used the Fine grid; the coarse
*           grid is used here to keep the test cheap.
*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

* Singlet, conventional integrals
&GATEWAY
  Coord = 3

    O  0.0000000000  0.0000000000  0.1173000000
    H  0.0000000000  0.7572000000 -0.4692000000
    H  0.1000000000 -0.7572000000 -0.4692000000
  Basis = 6-31G
  Group = NoSym
  NoCD

&SEWARD
  Grid input
    Grid = coarse
  End of Grid input

